# Admin page-section permissions

When adding a new CMS page or section in `src/data/sitePages.js` (for example `leadership.youthEscos`):

1. Add a Supabase migration that updates `public._sanitize_permissions` so the new section key is in `v_catalog`.
2. If it is a new page key, also add it to `admin_update_page_section` `v_allowed`.
3. Without this, ticking the permission checkbox appears to save but the key is stripped and the admin never gets access.

Known pattern: permissions are filtered server-side on save via `_sanitize_permissions`.
